+*mouse_raise_delay* <milliseconds>
+	Raise a floating window after the pointer stays over it for this duration.
+	Focus still follows the pointer immediately. Requires *focus_follows_mouse*
+	_yes_ or _always_. Zero disables delayed raising (the default); valid values
+	are 0 through 60000. Pointer leave, focus loss, geometry changes, dragging,
+	closing, fullscreen and session locking cancel a pending raise. Keyboard
+	focus alone never starts the timer. Already focused floating windows are
+	raised without changing keyboard focus or moving the pointer.
+
